<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fundi</span></b> , ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a sea-coast town of
				Latium</i>, <i>on the Appian Way</i>, <i>between Formiae and Tarracina</i>, now <i>Fondi</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				14, 6, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 41, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				5, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Galb. 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fundānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Fundi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 2, 25, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 2, 11, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				<i>near Fundi</i>, <i>whence the famous Caecuban
					wine</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 9, § 59</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, Amyclae, situated on the Lacus Fundanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					13, 115</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 6, 8, § 65</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fundāni</span></b> , <i>the
				inhabitants of Fundi</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				821</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fundānĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hercules,</span>”
				<i>who was worshipped at Fundi</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Flor. 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1539</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
